# The modules that the kernel of hd-kernel-desktop keeps of the config of Debian; make
# localmodconfig turns off every other module. What the config of Debian builds into the kernel
# stays. A line is one of:
#
#   <dir>/    every module of the directory <dir> of the kernel tree and of those below it
#   !<dir>/   none of the directory <dir> and of those below it, of a directory kept above
#   <module>  the module of that name, as lsmod prints it; the build stops when the kernel has no
#             module of that name, as a module or built in
#   <a>|<b>   the names of one module in different kernels, as in trixie and unstable; the
#             build stops when the kernel has none of them
#
# Everything but the drivers stays: file systems, network protocols and netfilter, crypto, and
# kvm. Of the drivers those of the hardware of the desktops and laptops (hyprdebian, iscsi1,
# hyprlap and beast, from the survey of lsmod of 2026-11-01) stay, the drivers of software that
# are not hardware, and whole directories of what people plug in: USB, HID, input, Bluetooth,
# webcams and USB sound and network.

